Mix.Tasks.Compile.All: a hook of beam.com after each compile

beam.com has NIF files in its zip (priv/nifs of the application
beam_com): native NIF objects for packages such as tailwind.com, whose
module loads priv/native/libtailwind_nif of its application. The Mix
build of beam.com ("beam.com DIR -o FILE") writes them into the priv
directories of the deps in the build path after its compile. A user
who runs Mix itself ("beam.com mix compile", "beam.com mix test") got
no files.

After a compile that has no error, call :beam_com_mix.compiled/0 when it
is exported. beam.com loads that module at the start of each tool of
Elixir. A usual install of Elixir has no such module, so nothing
changes there.

--- a/lib/mix/lib/mix/tasks/compile.all.ex
+++ b/lib/mix/lib/mix/tasks/compile.all.ex
@@ -79,6 +79,14 @@
       exit({:shutdown, 1})
     end
 
+    # A hook of beam.com (one file with OTP and Elixir): after a compile,
+    # :beam_com_mix.compiled/0 writes the NIF files of the file into the
+    # build path. A usual install has no module :beam_com_mix, and the
+    # module is not loaded in a plain run of this Mix.
+    if status != :error and function_exported?(:beam_com_mix, :compiled, 0) do
+      :beam_com_mix.compiled()
+    end
+
     if app_cache do
       Mix.AppLoader.write_cache(app_cache, Map.new(loaded_modules))
     end
